INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `author`, `category`, `tags`, `status`, `published_date`, `content`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `featured_image`) VALUES
(2, 'Seamless EMG & Motion Capture Integration with Delsys API and Vicon Nexus', 'Texon Corporation', 'Life Science', 'Biomechanics,EMG', 'published', '2026-01-01', '<p>The latest <strong>Delsys API integration with Vicon Nexus</strong> represents a major step forward in simplifying and strengthening EMG and motion capture workflows for biomechanics, clinical gait, sports performance, and research laboratories. With the updated Vicon Nexus integration (Nexus 2.16 and above), Delsys Trigno EMG systems now connect more seamlessly than ever using the Vicon Digital Device (VDD) framework, ensuring reliable real-time synchronization of muscle activity data with high-precision kinematic motion capture. A key improvement in this release is predictable and clearly ordered sensor numbering within Nexus, which significantly reduces setup time and configuration errors, especially in studies involving multiple EMG sensors. The integration also supports a broader range of Trigno sensors, enabling researchers to collect rich, synchronized datasets within a single software environment and export them effortlessly for advanced analysis. For labs and institutions using Vicon and Delsys together, this update delivers faster setup, fewer errors, and deeper insight into human movement—making it a highly valuable enhancement for modern motion analysis workflows.</p>', '2026-01-02 17:27:42', '2026-01-05 06:24:38', 'blogs/1767594278_Delsys + vicon.jpeg'),
(3, 'Why Calibration Is the Foundation of Accurate Motion Capture', 'Texon Corporation', 'Life Science', 'Motion capture,Biomechanis,Movement Science', 'published', '2026-01-02', '<p>At <strong>Texon Corporation</strong>, we know that successful motion capture starts long before you press <i>Record</i>. Whether you’re setting up a high-performance biomechanics lab, a sports science facility, or an entertainment production workflow, the accuracy and reliability of your motion capture data hinge on one often-overlooked step: <strong>camera calibration</strong>. In this blog, we explore how <strong>Vicon’s calibration devices</strong>, especially the new <strong>Active Wand</strong>, help you achieve world-class results with confidence and efficiency.&nbsp;</p><h3>&nbsp;</h3><h3>🎯 Why Calibration Matters</h3><p>Camera calibration is the foundational process that tells your motion capture system where each camera sits in 3D space relative to every other camera and the capture volume. Without a precise calibration, even the most advanced cameras and software — including Vicon Nexus — cannot accurately reconstruct movement in three dimensions. Poor calibration can lead to drift, scale errors, and unreliable datasets that compromise the integrity of your research or production.</p><p>In practice, calibration establishes the <strong>origin, orientation, and lens parameters</strong> of each camera so that the software can translate 2D camera images into accurate 3D marker locations. In Vicon systems, this calibration is typically performed at the start of each capture session or whenever the camera layout changes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><h3>🛠 Vicon’s Calibration Devices: Fast, Easy, and Reliable</h3><p>Vicon offers a range of calibration tools, but at the heart of every modern calibration workflow is the <strong>Active Wand</strong> — a purpose-built device that makes the calibration process faster and more consistent than traditional static wands.&nbsp;</p><h4><strong>What Makes the Active Wand Stand Out?</strong></h4><p>✔ <strong>Dual-Sided High-Intensity LEDs</strong><br>The Active Wand features LED markers on both sides, improving visibility across your camera array. This means more cameras see the wand at once, speeding up calibration and improving final accuracy.&nbsp;</p><p>✔ <strong>Up to 50% Faster Calibration</strong><br>Compared to legacy wands, the enhanced LED coverage and ergonomic design can <strong>reduce calibration time by nearly half</strong>, letting operators complete setup more quickly and consistently.&nbsp;</p><p>✔ <strong>Ergonomic and Practical Design</strong><br>The wand’s comfortable handle and USB-C rechargeable battery make it easier to use during long sessions — especially in large volumes or repeated calibration routines.</p><p>✔ <strong>Multiple Configurations</strong><br>Choose from an <strong>IR-only Active Wand</strong> for standard optical systems or an <strong>Active Wand Hybrid</strong> if your lab uses a mixed array of infrared (IR) and near-infrared (NIR) cameras. This flexibility supports both legacy and next-generation camera setups.</p><h3>&nbsp;</h3><h3>📈 Benefits for Your Customers</h3><p>Whether your end users are academic researchers, performance labs, or production studios, Vicon’s calibration tools deliver:</p><ul><li><strong>Consistent Data Quality</strong> — Reliable calibration leads to repeatable motion capture results.</li><li><strong>Reduced Setup Time</strong> — Faster calibration helps labs become more productive.</li><li><strong>Flexibility Across Systems</strong> — Support for both IR and hybrid camera setups ensures future-proof workflows.</li><li><strong>Operator Confidence</strong> — Clear LED visibility and ergonomic design make calibration less exhausting and more accurate.</li></ul>', '2026-01-02 17:36:35', '2026-01-05 06:24:17', 'blogs/1767594257_Untitled (908 x 1085 px).png'),
(4, 'Texon Corporation Completes Installation of 12 Vicon Valkyrie Cameras at SRMC Chennai for Cricket Bowling Analysis', 'Texon Corporation', 'Life Science', 'Biomechanics,Movement Scinence,Cricket,Sports Science,Vicon', 'published', '2025-12-25', '<h2>&nbsp;</h2><p><strong>Chennai, India —</strong> Texon Corporation is proud to announce the successful installation of <strong>12 Vicon Valkyrie VK8 motion capture cameras</strong> at the <strong>Sri Ramachandra Centre for Sports Science (SRCSS), SRMC Chennai</strong> — a major milestone in advancing sports biomechanics and performance analysis for cricket athletes.</p><p>SRCSS, part of the world-class <strong>Sri Ramachandra Institute of Higher Education and Research</strong>, is recognised as one of Asia’s leading sports science and biomechanics research centres. The facility supports multidisciplinary athlete development with modern labs, advanced sports medicine, physiotherapy, and nutrition services — and already features an extensive motion capture ecosystem, including Vicon systems used for cricket bowling action analysis and biomechanical testing.</p><h3><strong>Why This Installation Matters</strong></h3><p>Cricket bowling is a high-velocity, complex movement requiring detailed biomechanical insights to improve performance, reduce injury risk, and ensure compliance with bowling action regulations. Traditional video analysis can struggle to capture subtle joint rotations and rapid movements, especially in fast bowlers. The <strong>Vicon Valkyrie VK8</strong> technology provides <strong>industry-leading motion capture fidelity with high frame rates and precision</strong>, enabling researchers and coaches to analyse these movements with unparalleled clarity.</p><p>The <strong>VK8 model</strong> combines an <strong>8 MP sensor with up to 500 FPS native capture speed</strong>, offering the ideal balance of speed, resolution, and field coverage for sports applications such as cricket bowling, gait analysis, and high-velocity athletic motion.</p><h3><strong>Installation Overview</strong></h3><ul><li><strong>System:</strong> 12 × Vicon Valkyrie VK8 cameras + 2 FLIR Video Camera</li><li><strong>Location:</strong> CSS Biomechanics Lab, SRMC Chennai</li><li><strong>Application:</strong> Cricket bowling action capture and analysis</li><li><strong>Goal:</strong> Capture rapid motion data with sub-millimetre accuracy for performance profiling, technique improvement, and injury prevention</li></ul><p>The installation was carried out in close collaboration with <strong>Vicon OEM engineers Jinali and Adam Felipe</strong>, who provided <strong>in-depth demonstrations and training to the SRMC team</strong>, highlighting the <strong>latest features of Vicon software</strong> and best practices for capturing and analysing high-speed cricket bowling actions.</p><h3><strong>Celebrating a Benchmark Achievement</strong></h3><p>After the successful completion of the installation and training, Texon Corporation and the SRMC team <strong>cut a cake to commemorate this milestone</strong>, marking a memorable benchmark in India’s sports science ecosystem. The celebration reflected the strong partnership between Texon Corporation, Vicon, and SRMC in driving innovation in cricket performance analysis.</p><h3><strong>Technology That Delivers Performance</strong></h3><p>With the new Valkyrie VK8 cameras, SRMC can now:</p><ul><li>Analyse joint angles, angular velocities, and biomechanics with high precision</li><li>Detect subtle technical deviations impacting performance or injury risk</li><li>Provide evidence-based feedback to athletes and coaches</li><li>Conduct longitudinal research to monitor progress over time</li></ul><p>This upgrade enhances SRMC’s ability to track <strong>high-velocity actions</strong>, ensuring reliable, accurate, and repeatable motion data for elite cricket athletes.</p><h3><strong>Texon Corporation’s Commitment to Excellence</strong></h3><p>Texon Corporation continues to deliver <strong>world-class motion analysis solutions</strong> to India’s sports science, clinical, and research communities. By combining expert installation, OEM support, and ongoing training, we ensure that every technology investment translates into actionable insights and better outcomes for athletes and researchers alike.We congratulate the team at SRMC Chennai on this strategic upgrade and look forward to supporting their journey in performance analysis, injury prevention, and biomechanical research.</p>', '2026-01-02 17:52:11', '2026-01-05 06:24:02', 'blogs/1767594242_IMG_3613.JPG');

